= Using the hash classes =

* [#intro Introduction]
* [#md5 MD5]
* [#sha1 SHA1]
* [#sha256 SHA256]
* [#des DES]


[=#intro]
== Introduction ==

The [../classes/html/classmd5.html md5], [../classes/html/classsha1.html sha1], [../classes/html/classsha256.html sha256], and [../classes/html/classdes.html des] classes provide implementations of common hash algorithms.

All four classes inherit from the [../classes/html/classhash.html hash class] and share a common interface: append() to feed in data, getHash() to retrieve the hash, getHashSize() to get the hash length in bytes, and clear() to reset.  The isSupported() method can be used to determine if the hash algorithm is available on the current platform.

The md5, sha1, and sha256 classes produce binary hashes of different sizes.  The des class is different in that it requires a 2-character salt, and its output is printable ASCII, making it useful for the traditional unix password hashing scheme.


[=#md5]
== MD5 ==

The [../classes/html/classmd5.html md5 class] provides an MD5 implementation which produces a 128-bit (16-byte) hash.

The following example hashes a string, prints the result in hexadecimal, clears the hash, and hashes a different string.

